    {
        "content": "<p>Does someone know why in categories <code>C</code> with pullbacks, <code>Grp C</code> also has pullbacks, but <code>AddGrp C</code> does not?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CategoryTheory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Limits</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Category</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CartesianMonoidalCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">HasPullbacks</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HasPullbacks</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Grp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HasPullbacks</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">AddGrp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Error</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 624779528,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1789595422
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Probably <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Monoidal/Cartesian/GrpLimits.html#CategoryTheory.instHasLimitsOfShapeGrp\">CategoryTheory.instHasLimitsOfShapeGrp</a> needs <code>to_additive</code></p>",
        "id": 624883746,
        "sender_full_name": "Junyan Xu",
        "timestamp": 1789634146
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there any way of changing that? I am not sure sure how <code>to_additive</code> stuff need to done.</p>",
        "id": 624978705,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1789652623
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I just tried this on <a href=\"https://github.com/fpvandoorn/mathlib4/tree/to_additive_cat\">https://github.com/fpvandoorn/mathlib4/tree/to_additive_cat</a><br>\nIt mostly works fine, but there is at least one issue. <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.instHasLimitsOfShapeGrp#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.instHasLimitsOfShapeGrp</a> depends on <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.Grp.limitAux#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.Grp.limitAux</a>, which depends on <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Invertible#doc\">docs#Invertible</a>, which has no additive counterpart. So to do this we'd have to additivize <code>Invertible</code> to <code>Negatable</code> (you can add it to the list <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Mathlib.Tactic.ToAdditive.nameDict#doc\">docs#Mathlib.Tactic.ToAdditive.nameDict</a> so that <code>to_additive</code> generates the correct names itself). EDIT: Another option is to have a variant of <code>ofInvertible</code> that works in groups and doesn't mention <code>Invertible</code>.<br>\nFrom <code>to_additive</code>'s perspective there is no problem, it just requires every definition you use to also be additivized. Please adopt my branch if you want this to happen.<br>\ncc <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"648495\">@Christian Merten</span>, who mentioned something similar to me last week.</p>",
        "id": 624991339,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1789655208
    }
]